==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈskɛəsli/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈskɛɹsli/}}
* {{audio|en-us-scarcely.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|scarce|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{infl|en|adverb}}

# {{context|modal}} [[probably|Probably]] not.
#: ''One could '''scarcely''' find any trout in the stream without the stocking program.''
# {{context|modal}} [[certainly|Certainly]] not.
#: ''One could '''scarcely''' expect the man to know how to fly helicopter.''
# {{context|degree}} Almost not at all; by a small margin.
#: ''The room was '''scarcely''' larger than a closet.''
#* {{rfdate}} [[w:Baltasar Gracian|Baltasar Gracian]] (Philosopher)
#*: Nature '''scarcely''' ever gives us the very best; for that we must have recourse to art.

====Usage notes====
It is grammatically a negative word. It therefore collocates with [[ever]] rather than [[never]].
* Compare ''We '''scarcely''' ever eat fish.'' with ''We almost never eat fish.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|degree: by a small margin}} [[barely]], [[hardly]]

